# netsurf: fixes1135's cosmetic cap defers class churn instead of dropping it (patch 385)
# Generated 2026-11-07
# Base: seleron/vitabrowser (patch stack through 383)
#
# The "fixes1135 class-drop" logged since 372. After two class-only full
# rebuilds in a row, fixes1135 cleared the next single class mark's slot
# unrebuilt ("the styles were already applied by the JS setAttribute").
# Not so in this engine: style is computed when boxes are built, so the
# change stayed unrendered until some other change came. Its log line
# never appeared because diag.c drops every "LIFE reconvert" line as
# noise, and it ran BEFORE try_local, so even a change the local paths
# answer in a few ms was dropped.
#
# The cap still matters: patch 312's task flush fires the callback ~16 ms
# after every mutating task, which overrides fixes1024's escalating
# debounce, so a carousel's timer churn would otherwise cost a full
# rebuild per tick (the FLOOR aside).
#
#  - macos9_reconvert_cb: the check moves after try_local, just before
#    the full reconvert. Past the cap (still single class marks only, as
#    fixes1135), a class-only full rebuild waits until
#    RECONVERT_COSMETIC_DEFER_MS (= fixes1024's 6400 ms ceiling) after
#    the last full rebuild. Its slot stays pending and the callback is
#    re-armed for the window, so the page always converges, later marks
#    join the same batch (a multi-mark batch runs as before), and the
#    autotest's settle (page_reconvert_pending) waits for it.
#  - The log line is "LIFE cosmetic rebuild deferred %lu ms", outside the
#    noise prefix. macos9_reconvert_census_structural() replaces the two
#    copies of the census scan.
#
--- a/content/handlers/javascript/quickjs/macos9_reconvert.c	2026-11-07 00:29:15.176573172 +0000
